From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:54:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: skip the RCU wait on unauthorization without flush op

Since commit 06d6af4e1223 ("wifi: mac80211: flush STA queues on
unauthorization"), _sta_info_move_state() calls synchronize_net() when a
station loses AUTHORIZED on a driver with a set_key op, so that the
flush after it also covers frames that concurrent TX still queues.
NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION does not hold the RTNL, so the wait is a full
RCU grace period. Each SET_STATION that clears the authorized flag
blocks the caller for that time, once per station.

A driver without a flush or flush_sta op gets no flush, as
ieee80211_flush_queues() returns at once. The wait then keeps
no frame from the air: a frame that concurrent TX hands to the driver
can stay in its queue across a later key removal with or without it,
and the key itself is freed only after the synchronize_net() of
ieee80211_key_destroy() or __sta_info_destroy().

Only wait where the driver can flush.

Fixes: 06d6af4e1223 ("wifi: mac80211: flush STA queues on unauthorization")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
@@ -1519,9 +1519,12 @@ static int _sta_info_move_state(struct sta_info *sta,
 			 * (after ensuring concurrent TX completed) so we won't
 			 * transmit anything later unencrypted if/when keys are
 			 * also removed, which might otherwise happen depending
-			 * on how the hardware offload works.
+			 * on how the hardware offload works. Without a flush op
+			 * the wait keeps no queued frame off the air, as the
+			 * driver queue is not flushed.
 			 */
-			if (local->ops->set_key) {
+			if (local->ops->set_key &&
+			    (local->ops->flush_sta || local->ops->flush)) {
 				synchronize_net();
 				if (local->ops->flush_sta)
 					drv_flush_sta(local, sta->sdata, sta);
